@startuml provision-retire-recovery
title M-UM2: provision, retire and crash recovery (v0 design; v1 egress annotations)

participant "Configured caller\ninstaller / dispatcher / operator UID" as C
participant "sudo\ntrusted root transition" as S
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot; one invocation; no arguments" as M
database "Root-owned state\npolicy, ledger/cursor, lock, journal, audit\nv1 applied state" as R
participant "OS account backend / kernel\nmacOS or Linux; root operations" as O
database "Homes (account-owned)\nquarantine / metadata export (root-controlled)" as H
participant "swarma-credential-broker\nservice UID; owns bindings / leases" as B
participant "swarma-user-launcher\nroot; separate invocation" as L

note over C,L
  [[../spec/helper.md#43-usercreate Defining spec §4.3 create]], [[../spec/helper.md#44-userretire §4.4 retire]],
  [[../spec/helper.md#441-retirement-deletion-and-metadata-export §4.4.1 deletion/export]], [[../spec/helper.md#46-lock-journal-and-idempotency §4.6 recovery]].
  Current: unimplemented; v0 accounts, v1 firewall, v2 grant verification (§13).
  SH2+ joint admission gate I4 remains closed; dispatcher alone invokes the launcher (§§7, 14).
  Each helper request <= 16 KiB, one JSON document in 5 s (§2).
end note

== Before each invocation: intake, exclusive lock and recovery (§§2-3, 4.6) ==
C -> S: exact helper path; no args; helper-op/1 on stdin
S -> M: root; decimal trusted SUDO_UID identifies caller
break Invalid intake / role / ownership / quota; grants in v0/v1
  M --> C: refuse; closed operation schema
end
M -> R: acquire exclusive durable lock (shared by both binaries)
M -> R: read pending journal; compare actual OS objects before each action
alt Interrupted creation
  M -> O: roll back creation steps
  M -> H: roll back creation steps
else Interrupted retirement
  M -> M: resume forward from recorded steps (retirement sequence below)
end
M -> R: for mutations: check (caller principal, request_id) and canonical operation/args
break Mutation: same effect and same arguments
  M --> C: recorded result + target CURRENT state; do not repeat effect
end
break Mutation: same ID, different arguments
  M --> C: request_id_conflict
end
note over M,R
  Mutation sequences below describe new effects or pending recovery.
  effect.observe is a separate read-only invocation, outside the mutation replay/create path.
end note

== Read-only effect.observe (R-OBS, §§2, 4.5-4.6) ==
C -> S: effect.observe helper-op/1; original effect request_id,\noperation and canonical-argument digest (exact encoding unpublished)
S -> M: root; trusted SUDO_UID identifies observing caller
M -> R: acquire same exclusive lock; recovery first; authenticate original caller or operator;\nserialize observation with receiver journal and recovery
break Observing principal is neither original caller nor operator
  M --> C: refuse observation; no private journal exposure
end
M -> R: read caller/effect mapping, result, target state and rollback/removal evidence
M --> C: recorded (result + current state), pending, rolled_back,\nnot_recorded, unavailable or contradictory
note over C,R
  not_recorded requires complete authoritative coverage; expired/missing/unreadable evidence = unavailable.
  Mutation grant expiry does not prevent authenticated original-principal observation.
  Retain effect/removal evidence until original identities permanently inadmissible;
  concrete bounds and authoritative-coverage rule unpublished (§14 question 8).
  Observation never creates/relaunches; rolled_back/not_recorded do not authorise new create.
  Dispatcher maps recorded by current state; rolled_back/not_recorded -> known absent for effect only;
  pending/unavailable -> unknown; contradictory -> contradictory (§5).
end note

== user.create (§§4.1-4.3) ==
M -> R: choose round-robin UID/GID; new NEVER-REUSED generation
M -> O: check directory service and ledger availability;
M -> O: before UID reuse check platform and temporary areas for owned files
break Dirty UID / unmanaged name or home / exhausted range
  M --> C: uid_not_clean / user_exists_unmanaged / home_exists_unmanaged / range_exhausted
end
M -> R: journal planned/completed steps before acting; state creating
M -> O: create account + same-name primary group; no supplementary groups;
M -> O: locked password, no login shell, hidden; exact UID/GID/home
M -> H: descriptor-relative empty home; account owner; mode 0700
opt v1 profile requires enforcement
  M -> O: install denial before activation / first launch
  note over M,O: Whole matrix without evidence refuses fw_unsupported (§8); creation failure rolls back.
end
alt Creation fails or crashes at a step boundary
  note over M,R: Crash stops invocation; next invocation recovers first (§4.6).
  M -> O: roll back creation, comparing OS objects with journal
  M -> H: roll back creation
  note over M,H: Exact per-step rollback order / firewall rollback details: unspecified in spec §§4.3, 4.6, 8.
else Creation succeeds
  M -> R: persist active; record result and audit line
  M --> C: username, UID/GID, home, generation, state active
end

== user.retire (§4.4): forward recovery only ==
note over C,M
  Dispatcher normally unbinds before retirement (§10).
  Create/bind/launch/stop/unbind/retire have distinct effect IDs;
  retry each effect with its same ID (§5).
  Retirement deletes the home; no archive/delete/keep selector (§4.4.1).
  Separate explicit operator home retention: confidentiality not guaranteed; format unpublished.
end note
M -> R: journal steps; persist retiring FIRST (commit point)
note over L,B: Launcher refuses new starts; broker refuses leases for retiring generation.
M -> B: ask to end generation binding where present
M -> O: stop per-user service domain where available;
M -> O: terminate every UID process; verify quiet period
break Processes remain or quiescence not established
  M --> C: processes_remain for remaining processes; stay retiring; retry later
  note over M,O: Unknown/failed observation cannot establish absence (§4.7);\nexact retirement observation error / quiet-period duration: unspecified in spec §4.4.
end
note over M,O: v1 denial remains in place throughout home and account cleanup.
M -> H: same-filesystem move into quarantine
M -> R: journal declared-key destruction under shared lock
M -> H: destroy declared keys through trusted descriptors BEFORE walk
break Key destruction failed or unknown
  M -> R: audit outcome without secrets; remain retiring
  M --> C: retirement pending; no walk
end
note over M,H: Recovery confirms destruction or prior absence before continuing.\nDeclared paths / format unpublished (§14 question 6); never follow links.
M -> H: descriptor-relative delete ALL home content/names/links;\nunlink symlinks without following them
break Required deletion failed, partial or unknown
  M -> R: audit outcome without secrets; remain retiring
  M --> C: retirement pending; unreadability is not absence
end
opt Closed metadata schema and provenance published and qualified (§14 question 6)
  M -> R: generate metadata only from trusted service records; validate closed schema
  M -> H: publish root 0600 metadata export in root 0700 archive directory
  note over M,H: No agent-controlled strings/names/links/bodies; no copying/scanning home.\nUnknown provenance/schema failure prevents export publication (§4.4.1).
end
M -> R: audit quiescence, key destruction, deletion and export outcomes; no secrets
M -> O: remove owned files from system and per-user temporary areas
M -> O: remove account and group
opt v1
  M -> O: remove firewall rules LAST
end
M -> R: persist removed (generation retained forever); result + audit
note over M,H
  archive.sweep: metadata exports ONLY; age, then oldest until total bound.
  At every retirement and from a daily root timer; preserve live effect/tombstone evidence.
  Installer/operator authority (§§3, 4.4.1).
  Export schema/naming/bounds and audit encoding unpublished (§14 question 6).
  Timer process details beyond root / sweep retry unspecified in spec §4.4.1.
end note
M --> C: username, generation, state removed
note over M,R: Crash after retiring commit: next invocation compares OS objects to journal\nand resumes forward; no rollback to active (§§4.2, 4.6).
note over C,B
  Account retirement is separate from identity revocation (§4.4).
  Dispatcher may revoke only recorded one-shot identities after retirement;
  standing identities remain; only operator may revoke with signed record.
end note
@enduml
